    "status": "agent_returned",
    "response": "I didn't find an improvement. The best run is still the prior reference, `20261031T142814768185Z-m-eurosat-manual`, at 0.870 validation accuracy.\n\n- **Baseline reproduction:** I re-ran the frozen recipe (ResNet18, lr 0.01, 10 epochs). It scored 0.870 accuracy and 0.868 macro-F1, identical to the prior best. Ties keep the prior best, so it wasn't promoted.\n- **Epoch increase (rejected):** My first idea was 30 epochs, since 630 steps looked undertrained. The tool rejected it because 10 epochs is the contract cap. No training ran.\n- **Retry mistake:** I then submitted the lr change with `retry_of` set by mistake, and the tool rejected it as not retryable. I resubmitted it as a normal run. That used the one eligible retry slot at most, and no training was lost.\n- **Learning-rate change:** I lowered lr from 0.01 to 0.003, expecting more stable convergence. It scored 0.862 accuracy and 0.861 macro-F1, so I rejected it. Class 4 recall fell to 0.85 (from 0.99). The last-epoch validation was worse, at 0.822, so training was not stable at the end either.\n- **Verification:** The prediction check on the prior best checkpoint passed.\n\nThe remaining errors are mostly between classes 0, 3 and 6. Longer training is not allowed. A next step could be changing something else, such as weight decay or augmentation, or averaging over several seeds. With a 1,000-image validation set, a gap of 0.8 points is within noise.\n\nI never touched the test split.\n"
